# Vercel uploads the working directory, NOT the git index — it reads this file,
# not .gitignore. Without these rules `vercel deploy` tries to upload the 27GB
# of camera masters in public/media/ and fails outright on Vercel's 2GB
# per-file limit (one master is 5.78GB).
#
# Production deploys normally come from the connected GitHub repo, which only
# ever contains the committed derivatives, so this matters for manual CLI
# deploys.
#
# Keep in sync with the matching block in .gitignore.
public/media/*
!public/media/placeholder

# Logo masters: 16667px square, ~1.2MB each, and never served. The site points
# at the derived public/brand/lumen-haul-mark.png and the icons in src/app,
# both cut by scripts/encode-brand.mjs. The masters stay in git as the source
# to re-cut from; they have no business in a deploy.
#
# Matched by the stable master-* prefix rather than by the exports' own names,
# which change with every logo revision — this rule silently stopped matching
# once already when the files were renamed.
public/brand/master-*
